[
    {
        "content": "<p>While working on a project, Claude found a case where <code>lia</code> fails to deduce a simple fact from obvious existing hypotheses, but <code>omega</code> succeeds. I got it to minimize to two Mathlib imports, but further minimization seems hard -- some parts of the precise shapes of the things imported from Mathlib seem to be essential. In the end, it comes down to a local hypothesis of a certain (rather special) form confusing <code>grind</code>. (This may be related to similar observations others have made from time to time.)</p>\n<p>Here is the reproducer that Claude gave me after a few rounds of minimizing:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RingTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AdjoinRoot</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RingTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Quotient</span>\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">Minimal reproduction: a trivial `natDegree = 2` goal on which `omega` succeeds but `lia`</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">(a `grind` wrapper) fails.  Import-minimized and bisected from a real failure in</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">`Heights.EllipticCurve.SelmerGroup` (`mk_eq_one_iff_forall_evalRoot_nonneg`).</span>\n\n<span class=\"cm\">`grind` case-splits the subtype `p` into `⟨val, property⟩` and then treats `↑⟨val, property⟩` as</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">a term disconnected from `val`/`↑p`, so `cutsat` sees two copies of `natDegree` and cannot close</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">what is pure `ℕ` arithmetic (`0 &lt; n`, `n ≤ 2`, `n ≠ 1` ⊢ `n = 2`).  This is a `grind` issue, not a</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">`lia`-specific one: plain `grind` (E-matching enabled) fails here too.</span>\n\n<span class=\"cm\">Essential ingredients — removing any one makes the tactic succeed:</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">* `myEvalRoot`, a def GENERAL over `{K : Type*} [Field K]` returning an `AlgEquiv` whose domain</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  `AdjoinRoot (X - C e)` depends on the argument `e`, used in `h` at a CONCRETE field (`ℚ`).  A</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  fixed domain (`K ≃ₐ[K] K`), a plain `Equiv`/`RingEquiv`/`MulEquiv`, an `ℚ`-specific def, a plain</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  general function, an *arbitrary field variable* `[Field F]` for `ℚ`, or an instance-carrying</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  `structure` STUB in place of the real `AlgEquiv` all stop the reproduction.  (The order on the</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  field is irrelevant — an equality hypothesis suffices.)</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">* `h1` obtained by applying to `p.2` (the `Irreducible` field of the subtype) a lemma whose type</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  mentions `natDegree` (`Irreducible.natDegree_pos`).  Giving `h1` directly, dropping `h`, or</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  stubbing `ℚ[X]`/`Irreducible`/`natDegree` all make it succeed.</span>\n\n<span class=\"cm\">So both Mathlib ingredients are needed together: it cannot be stubbed to zero imports.</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">The three copies below share a signature; only the finishing tactic differs.</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Polynomial</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- `h` is deliberately unused by the succeeding tactics (copies 1 and 3) — its mere presence is</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- what makes `lia` fail in copy 2.</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unusedVariables</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myEvalRoot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">AdjoinRoot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₐ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">quotientSpanXSubCAlgEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- (1) `omega` closes it.</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myEvalRoot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Irreducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">})</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree_pos</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">omega</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- (2) `lia` fails; the error is captured (and thus absorbed) by `#guard_msgs`.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: `grind` failed</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">case grind</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">h : ∀ (e : ℚ), (myEvalRoot e) 1 = 0</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">p : { q // Irreducible q }</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">hd : (↑p).natDegree ≠ 1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">h2 : (↑p).natDegree ≤ 2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">h1 : 0 &lt; (↑p).natDegree</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">h_1 : ¬(↑p).natDegree = 2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">val : ℚ[X]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">property : Irreducible val</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">h_2 : ⟨val, ⋯⟩ = p</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ False</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">[grind] Goal diagnostics</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [facts] Asserted facts</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] ∀ (e : ℚ), (myEvalRoot e) 1 = 0</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] ¬(↑p).natDegree = 1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] (↑p).natDegree ≤ 2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] 1 ≤ (↑p).natDegree</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] ¬(↑p).natDegree = 2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] Irreducible val</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] ⟨val, ⋯⟩ = p</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [eqc] True propositions</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] Irreducible val</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] 1 ≤ (↑p).natDegree</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] (↑p).natDegree ≤ 2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] ∀ (e : ℚ), (myEvalRoot e) 1 = 0</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [eqc] False propositions</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] (↑p).natDegree = 1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [prop] (↑p).natDegree = 2</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [eqc] Equivalence classes</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [eqc] {p, ⟨val, ⋯⟩}</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [eqc] {val, ↑p}</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">      [eqc] {↑⟨val, ⋯⟩}</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [cases] Case analyses</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [cases] [1/1]: p</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">      [cases] source: Initial goal</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [ematch] E-matching patterns</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [thm] h: [@DFunLike.coe (AlgEquiv `[ℚ] _ `[ℚ] `[Field.toSemifield.toCommSemiring] _ `[Field.toSemifield.toDivisionSemiring.toSemiring] _ `[Algebra.id</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">            ℚ]) _ _ _ (@myEvalRoot `[ℚ] `[Rat.instField] #0) (@OfNat.ofNat _ `[1] _)]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [thm] h: [@myEvalRoot `[ℚ] `[Rat.instField] #0]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [thm] Subtype.property: [@Subtype.val #2 #1 #0]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [thm] natDegree_natCast: [@natDegree #2 #1 (@NatCast.natCast (Polynomial _ _) _ #0)]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [thm] Set.subset_def: [@LE.le _ _ #1 #0]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [cutsat] Assignment satisfying linear constraints</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [assign] (↑p).natDegree := 0</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [assign] (↑p).natDegree := 1</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [limits] Thresholds reached</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    [limit] maximum number of E-matching rounds has been reached, threshold: `(ematch := 0)` -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myEvalRoot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Irreducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">})</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree_pos</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">lia</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- (3) `clear h; lia` closes it (dropping the offending hypothesis).</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myEvalRoot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Irreducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">})</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">2</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natDegree_pos</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">clear</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">lia</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
